description: Formatted plain text keeps the lines of code blocks and renders lists without blank lines
impact-type: compatibility-break

Formatted plain text output used to collapse a multi-line code block onto one line and separate list items with blank lines. Code blocks now keep their line breaks, and each list item is a line starting with `  - ` instead of `* `.

The command line help is the first to benefit. The same readable output comes without any change to:

* `<$wikify output="formattedtext">` in wikitext
* `wiki.renderTiddler("text/plain-formatted", ...)` in JavaScript
* server-side plugins that read `formattedTextContent` of fakedom nodes

Text and HTML output are unchanged.

Code that parses formatted list output needs a small update:

* Match the item prefix `  - ` instead of `* `. For example, a filter step `removeprefix[* ]` becomes `removeprefix[  - ]`, and a JavaScript pattern `/^\* /` becomes `/^  - /`
* Split items on single newlines, since there are no longer blank lines between them

Workarounds that rebuilt collapsed code blocks can be removed.
